# What Prettier does not format, read by `pnpm format` and `pnpm check:format`.
#
# Patterns are read the way .gitignore reads them, but relative to this file – so a
# pattern with a slash in it resolves under config/prettier/ and matches nothing. A
# bare name matches at any depth; anything with a path in it needs a leading **/ to
# escape this directory.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml
.pnpm-store/

# Build output. Gradle writes the root project's problems report to `build/` no
# matter where the subprojects are told to build, so that one directory escapes
# `.build/` – the same exception `.gitignore` carries.
.build/
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Swift and Kotlin. Prettier has no parser for either and skips them in silence;
# saying so here is what keeps "check:format passed" from reading as "these were
# checked". SwiftFormat and ktlint own them instead.
*.swift
*.kt
*.kts

# Shell. Prettier has no parser for it either, and there is no shell formatter in
# the toolchain – these are held to review rather than to a tool.
*.sh

# SVG is XML, so the XML plugin would take it – but every SVG here already has an
# owner: svgo rewrites the icons through `pnpm format:svg`, and Structurizr writes
# the diagrams through `pnpm build:arch`. A second formatter would fight both.
*.svg

# Generated, and owned by the tool that writes them. Editing any of these by
# hand is a mistake, so formatting them is one too.
**/apps/apple/Campfire.xcodeproj/
**/apps/apple/config/generated/
**/apps/android/gradle/wrapper/
**/apps/android/gradlew
**/apps/android/gradlew.bat

# The compiled workspace Structurizr local writes while a view is arranged. The
# tool owns its shape, and a Prettier pass would rewrite a file the next layout
# session rewrites back.
**/docs/architecture/workspace.json

# Xcode-managed asset catalogs and the app icon, written by Xcode and Icon
# Composer. Both emit `"key" : value`, so a Prettier pass and the next icon edit
# would rewrite each other forever.
**/apps/apple/assets/

# What the mock copies in from elsewhere: the auth service's refresh script, byte for
# byte from wsj27-auth-api so the keep-alive loop is the real one, and the design
# system's display face. Formatting either would make it a copy that no longer compares
# equal to its source.
**/tools/mock/static/

# Agent scratch and the reference material under study – gitignored working files.
temp/
**/.agents/specs/
